  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nShowers continue to drift through parts of northeast Montana this\nafternoon. With daytime heating, some storms could also pop up,\nbut consistent cloud cover across the region likely would be an\ninhibiting factor for any strong to severe storms.\n\nAnother disturbance may move in from central Montana Thursday \nnight and exit Friday, then the heat is on with temps reaching the\n90s to around 100 and going further Saturday with only the \nnortheast zones reaching the 90s while the rest of the CWA is \nexpected to reach 100 to 110.\n\nAn excessive heat watch has been issued for the entire CWA\nSaturday through Saturday night as overnight temps will only fall\ninto the 70s then rebound into the low to mid 90s Sunday.\n\nBut northwest winds ramp significantly Sunday in the wake of a \nfrontal system. Winds of 15 to 25 mph with possible gusts to 40 \nmph are possible. Combined with very low humidity (~10% in many \nplaces), this will likely be a critical day for Fire Weather. But \nwinds do look to back off late in the day that could bring some \nrelief.\n\nBy Monday, afternoon high temperatures across the region could be\nin the 70s and 80s, which would be a 20-30 degree cooldown from \nSaturday. A slow warmup is expected thereafter.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather Friday and Saturday. \nConfidence is increasing for critical fire weather conditions  \nSunday. Low confidence in timing any showers and thunderstorms.\n\nNo major deviations from the base forecast were made for this\niteration.\n\nCliff",
